# A cast whose source or target is a DEFERRED indexed access (`T[K]`) is
# conceded outright (indexed/031): tsc rejects one only when
# `getBaseConstraintOfType` fully reduces the access, which needs the object
# constraint to answer for every key the index constraint admits. Reducing it
# structurally instead — substituting each parameter's constraint — also
# collapses the shapes tsc leaves deferred, and then rejects casts tsc accepts
# (`s as T[K]` under `T extends { a: number; b: number }`, among others).
# Re-measured 2026-08-02 by removing the concession from `castComparableRec`:
# ztsc then reports SIX TS2352 on `indexed/031`, whose oracle snapshot is
# empty — six false rejections to gain the one true report below. Trading a
# deterministic under-report for that is the standing policy direction.
# (`castComparableRec`'s own doc comment still says "four more shapes
# besides", the count measured when the concession landed; the case grew a
# sixth cast since.) Line 14, whose operands are not deferred, still reports.
indexed/032_cast_to_deferred_indexed_access_negatives.ts  -TS2352 8

# TS2344 decides a written type argument against its parameter's constraint
# when that constraint is a PRIMITIVE OR LITERAL SET (a primitive, a literal,
# an enum member, `never`, or a union/intersection of those) or a STRUCTURAL
# type — an object type, or a reference to an interface/class/alias (see
# `decidableConstraintSet`). The structural arm was closed until the relation
# could carry a negative verdict on the recursive `this`-typed generic
# families it is mostly used with; it opened once both halves of the zod
# counter-example were fixed and pinned (`assignability/078` for measured
# variance, `assignability/080` for the growing-instantiation guard), with
# `bench/parity_sweep.sh` at 0 under / 0 excess on all eight packages as the
# evidence.
#
# What stays undecided is an argument that is still a type VARIABLE or a
# DEFERRED node — an `infer` binder, an unreduced conditional / indexed
# access / `keyof`. Those are not sets ztsc can enumerate, and every one of
# the 130+ false TS2344s the unguarded check invented across the corpus was
# one of them. Line 26 is that shape — a DEFERRED ARGUMENT, not a structural
# constraint: the argument is `T["k"]`, an indexed access into a still-free
# `T`, which tsc decides through its constraint machinery and ztsc does not.
# Nothing about the structural arm (open since B1) bears on it.
instantiation/052_type_arg_constraint_structural.ts  -TS2344 26

# A REVERSE MAPPED TYPE. tsc's `inferToMappedType` has two branches. ztsc
# models the one keyed on a type-parameter key set (`Record<infer N, V>`; see
# `mappedInferShape` and case 047) and declines the HOMOMORPHIC one,
# `{ [P in keyof U]: X }` — reached both by writing it that way and by
# instantiating `Pick<U, keyof U>`, which is immich's
# `RepositoryInterface<T>`. tsc answers it with
# `inferTypeForHomomorphicMappedType`, synthesizing a reverse mapped type;
# ztsc has no such type, so the binder is left unowned and the conditional
# keeps its false branch (`never`) — all four lines are missed errors.
#
# Both approximations were measured on immich (gated at 0) and both are false
# positives, the direction the policy above refuses:
#
#   * OWN the binder without matching it -> it resolves to `unknown`, which
#     relates to almost anything, so the conditional takes its TRUE branch with
#     a meaningless value: 1 false TS2345 (`Argument of type 'unknown'`).
#   * BIND it to the source -> exact only for the identity template `U[P]`, and
#     even then not free: `As<T>` became the real repository type, so 47 casts
#     that had been comparing against `never` started comparing for real and
#     ztsc's COMPARABLE relation rejected every one
#     (`Mocked<RepositoryInterface<X>> as X`, which tsc accepts): 0 -> 47 false
#     TS2352.
#
# Closing this needs reverse mapped types AND that comparable-relation gap.
# Measured 2026-08-10.
conditional/048_infer_through_homomorphic_key_set_deferred.ts  -TS2322 31
conditional/048_infer_through_homomorphic_key_set_deferred.ts  -TS2322 37
conditional/048_infer_through_homomorphic_key_set_deferred.ts  -TS2322 41
