# LEGACY (`experimentalDecorators`) decorator resolution, the parts ztsc does
# not do. The call itself IS resolved now (`checkLegacyDecoratorSig`, and
# 010_legacy_signature_failures pins every code, span and wording it produces —
# outline's sixty TS1240s among them). What is left out is, in order of the
# case's own numbering:
#
#   * an OVERLOAD SET where every candidate fails (51). tsc reports the last
#     candidate's argument error inside a nested "No overload matches this
#     call." / "The last overload gave the following error." chain, a second
#     reporting shape on top of the head message; ztsc resolves a single
#     signature only.
#   * a GENERIC decorator (52). Its parameters are only judgeable after the
#     type arguments are inferred from the synthesized tuple, and this path
#     does no inference.
#   * a NON-CALLABLE decorator (53) — tsc's "This expression is not callable."
#     Its guard is `isUntypedFunctionCall`, i.e. assignability to the global
#     `Function`, so a `Function`-typed decorator must stay silent while a
#     plain object must not; the distinction is not modelled.
#   * TS1329, a decorator FACTORY left uncalled (54). This one is not just
#     skipped but explicitly suppressed: the arity failure ztsc would
#     otherwise report is the WRONG diagnostic for the shape (tsc's
#     `isPotentiallyUncalledDecorator` runs ahead of the arity check), so the
#     guard is in `checkLegacyDecoratorSig` and the missing report is the
#     price of not inventing a different one.
#   * a UNION-typed decorator (55), whose call signature is the union's
#     combined one (parameters intersected).
#   * the decorator's RETURN type (56) — TS1270/TS1271, a separate family from
#     the signature codes and a separate check.
#   * PARAMETER decorators (58, 59): TS1239 is unreachable because the parser
#     DISCARDS a legacy parameter decorator's expression rather than hanging it
#     off the parameter (`parseParam`), so there is no node to resolve. This is
#     a frontend gap, not a checker one.
#
# Every entry is a missed error on a shape the oracle rejects; none of them can
# turn into a false positive, which is why the resolution landed without them.
